feat: campaigns, evergreen recycling, approval workflow, slot categories, CSV import

Five Buffer/Hootsuite-class capabilities on the social scheduler, one slice:

- CAMPAIGNS: a named series (Campaign model, workspace-scoped, unique name)
  with its own utm_campaign stamped at send — a campaign's tag beats the
  workspace-wide one. Managed on /social (create, archive, delete via the
  deletable registry — posts survive deletion, they just unlink).

- EVERGREEN RECYCLING: flag a post + cooldown; once it has actually gone out,
  the social sweep clones it into a free queue slot (7-day fill horizon,
  5/sweep cap, skips disconnected accounts, one clone in flight per source).
  Clones are ordinary scheduled posts carrying recycledFromId — every send
  keeps its own honest per-leg history. OPT-IN per workspace
  (social:evergreen_fill, default off): automatic posting is never a surprise.

- APPROVAL WORKFLOW (opt-in, social:require_approval): non-admin posts are
  held as drafts until approved. Enforced server-side in publishSocialPost,
  the sweep's claim (an OR over null/approved — NOT IN would silently exclude
  every normal null row), queue, drag and post-now paths; duplicates re-enter
  review so copying can't dodge it. Approve honors the requested time;
  request-changes carries a note; editing a sent-back post resubmits.
  New notification kind approval_decided; approval_needed notifies admins.

- SLOT CATEGORIES: Buffer-style lanes on posting slots. One matching rule in
  pickFreeSlot (own category → general; general → any) so nothing strands.

- CSV IMPORT: up to 200 rows (text, scheduledAt, networks, campaign,
  category, evergreen, recycleEveryDays), per-row errors, media-required
  networks dropped per row with a note, approval workflow applies.

Composer gains campaign/category/evergreen controls; /social gains Campaigns,
Workflow and CSV cards plus an always-visible Awaiting-approval section; the
schedule editor takes a category per slot. Help tips + 4 Help-centre entries.

Pure-function probes pass (slot matching 6/6, UTM override 3/3). Migration
20260804010000 adds Campaign + columns; deploy applies it on boot.

